@Llcoolsouder But this won't allocate 3D pitched memory.

@czgdp1807 I am not sure if a generic `GpuMatND` should be implemented or if a proxy object (like the one described in #16433) must be used.

The `GpuMat` interface was for C++98. I think it is better to have a C++11 interface (what's the point of having C++98 interface when OpenCV has already moved to C++11). The only problem would be that the interface would not be compatible with the `GpuMat`'s interface. It's just my opinion.
